## HTTP Methods

### GET (Read)
```
GET /api/users                          # Retrieve all users
GET /api/users/123                      # Retrieve specific user
GET /api/users?page=2&limit=10         # Retrieve with filters
```
- **Safe**: Doesn't modify server state
- **Idempotent**: Same result on multiple calls
- **Cacheable**: Results can be cached
- **No body**: GET requests don't have request bodies

### 🔑 GET - KEY POINTS & NOTES
```
✓ Always use GET for retrieving data
✓ Use query parameters for filtering, sorting, pagination
✓ Can be cached aggressively (browser, CDN)
✗ Never send sensitive data in query parameters (visible in URL)
✗ Avoid GET with request body (not standard, some servers reject)
⚠️ Limit query string length (browsers: ~2000 chars, servers vary)
```

### 💡 PRACTICAL EXAMPLES
```javascript
// JavaScript - Fetch API
const fetchUsers = async (page = 1, status = 'active') => {
  const url = new URL('https://api.example.com/users');
  url.searchParams.append('page', page);
  url.searchParams.append('status', status);
  
  const response = await fetch(url, {
    method: 'GET',
    headers: {
      'Authorization': 'Bearer token123',
      'Accept': 'application/json'
    }
  });
  
  return response.json();
};

// Angular HttpClient
import { HttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';

constructor(private http: HttpClient) {}

getUsers(page: number, status: string) {
  const params = new HttpParams()
    .set('page', page)
    .set('status', status);
  
  return this.http.get('/api/users', { params });
}

// React Query
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';

function useUsers(page, status) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ['users', page, status],
    queryFn: () => 
      fetch(`/api/users?page=${page}&status=${status}`)
        .then(r => r.json()),
    staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000 // Cache for 5 minutes
  });
}
```

