```
POST /api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com"
}
```
- **Unsafe**: Creates new resources
- **Non-idempotent**: Multiple calls create multiple resources
- **With body**: Contains resource data
- **Returns**: 201 Created with Location header

### 🔑 POST - KEY POINTS & NOTES
```
✓ Always return 201 Created with Location header
✓ Return created resource in response body
✓ Validate all input before processing
✗ Never make POST idempotent by accident (implement idempotency keys if needed)
⚠️ POST can be used for non-CRUD operations (e.g., /search, /export)
⚠️ Large payloads: Set timeout and size limits
```

### 💡 PRACTICAL EXAMPLES
```javascript
// Node.js/Express
app.post('/api/users', async (req, res) => {
  // Validate input
  const { name, email } = req.body;
  if (!name || !email) {
    return res.status(400).json({
      error: { code: 'VALIDATION_ERROR', message: 'Name and email required' }
    });
  }

  try {
    // Check for duplicates
    const existing = await User.findOne({ email });
    if (existing) {
      return res.status(409).json({
        error: { code: 'DUPLICATE_EMAIL', message: 'Email already exists' }
      });
    }

    // Create user
    const user = await User.create({ name, email });

    // Return 201 with Location header
    res.status(201)
      .location(`/api/users/${user.id}`)
      .json({
        success: true,
        data: user
      });
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({
      error: { code: 'SERVER_ERROR', message: error.message }
    });
  }
});

// Angular
createUser(user: User) {
  return this.http.post<User>('/api/users', user).pipe(
    tap(newUser => {
      // Update local state
      this.users = [...this.users, newUser];
    })
  );
}

// React with error handling
const createUser = async (userData) => {
  try {
    const response = await fetch('/api/users', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify(userData)
    });

    if (response.status === 201) {
      const user = await response.json();
      const locationHeader = response.headers.get('Location');
      console.log('User created at:', locationHeader);
      return user;
    } else if (response.status === 409) {
      throw new Error('Email already exists');
    } else {
      throw new Error('Failed to create user');
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error:', error);
    throw error;
  }
};
```

