### PUT (Replace/Update)
```
PUT /api/users/123
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "jane@example.com"
}
```
- **Unsafe**: Modifies resource
- **Idempotent**: Multiple calls with same data produce same result
- **Full replacement**: Updates entire resource
- **Should include all fields**: Send complete representation

### 🔑 PUT - KEY POINTS & NOTES
```
✓ Idempotent - safe to retry multiple times
✓ Replace entire resource - send all fields
✓ Return 200 OK with updated resource or 204 No Content
✓ Validate that all required fields are present
✗ Don't use PUT for partial updates (use PATCH instead)
✗ Can create resource if it doesn't exist (but usually avoid this)
⚠️ Consider using If-Match header with ETag for concurrency control
```

### 💡 PRACTICAL EXAMPLES
```javascript
// Node.js/Express - Full update with validation
app.put('/api/users/:id', async (req, res) => {
  const { id } = req.params;
  const { name, email, phone, address } = req.body;

  // Validate all required fields
  if (!name || !email) {
    return res.status(400).json({
      error: { code: 'VALIDATION_ERROR', message: 'Name and email required' }
    });
  }

  try {
    // Check if user exists
    const user = await User.findById(id);
    if (!user) {
      return res.status(404).json({
        error: { code: 'NOT_FOUND', message: 'User not found' }
      });
    }

    // Check for email conflict (if email changed)
    if (user.email !== email) {
      const existing = await User.findOne({ email });
      if (existing) {
        return res.status(409).json({
          error: { code: 'DUPLICATE_EMAIL', message: 'Email already exists' }
        });
      }
    }

    // Perform full update
    const updated = await User.findByIdAndUpdate(
      id,
      { name, email, phone, address },
      { new: true, runValidators: true }
    );

    res.status(200).json({
      success: true,
      data: updated
    });
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({
      error: { code: 'SERVER_ERROR', message: error.message }
    });
  }
});

// Angular - PUT with optimistic updates
updateUser(id: string, user: User) {
  return this.http.put<User>(`/api/users/${id}`, user).pipe(
    tap(updated => {
      // Optimistically update local state
      const index = this.users.findIndex(u => u.id === id);
      if (index !== -1) {
        this.users[index] = updated;
      }
    }),
    catchError(error => {
      // Revert on error
      this.loadUsers(); // Reload from server
      throw error;
    })
  );
}

// React - PUT with ETag for concurrency control
const updateUserWithETag = async (userId, userData, etag) => {
  const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${userId}`, {
    method: 'PUT',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      'If-Match': etag  // Optimistic locking
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(userData)
  });

  if (response.status === 412) {
    throw new Error('Resource was modified, please refresh and retry');
  }

  return response.json();
};
```

