### DELETE (Remove)
```
DELETE /api/users/123
```
- **Unsafe**: Removes resource
- **Idempotent**: Multiple calls have same effect
- **No body**: Doesn't require request body
- **Returns**: 204 No Content (usually)

### 🔑 DELETE - KEY POINTS & NOTES
```
✓ Idempotent - safe to retry multiple times
✓ Usually return 204 No Content (no response body)
✓ Can return 200 OK with deletion confirmation if needed
✓ Consider soft deletes instead of hard deletes (better for audit trails)
✗ Be careful with cascading deletes (document dependencies)
⚠️ Implement authorization checks to prevent unauthorized deletions
⚠️ Consider requiring confirmation for sensitive deletions
```

### 💡 PRACTICAL EXAMPLES
```javascript
// Node.js/Express - Hard delete
app.delete('/api/users/:id', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => {
  const { id } = req.params;

  try {
    const user = await User.findById(id);
    if (!user) {
      return res.status(404).json({
        error: { code: 'NOT_FOUND', message: 'User not found' }
      });
    }

    // Check authorization
    if (req.user.id !== id && req.user.role !== 'admin') {
      return res.status(403).json({
        error: { code: 'FORBIDDEN', message: 'Cannot delete this user' }
      });
    }

    await User.findByIdAndDelete(id);

    // Return 204 No Content
    res.status(204).send();
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({
      error: { code: 'SERVER_ERROR', message: error.message }
    });
  }
});

// Node.js/Express - Soft delete (safer)
app.delete('/api/users/:id', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => {
  const { id } = req.params;

  try {
    const user = await User.findById(id);
    if (!user) {
      return res.status(404).json({
        error: { code: 'NOT_FOUND', message: 'User not found' }
      });
    }

    // Soft delete
    await User.findByIdAndUpdate(id, {
      deletedAt: new Date(),
      active: false
    });

    res.status(200).json({
      success: true,
      message: 'User deleted successfully'
    });
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({
      error: { code: 'SERVER_ERROR', message: error.message }
    });
  }
});

// Angular
deleteUser(id: string) {
  return this.http.delete(`/api/users/${id}`).pipe(
    tap(() => {
      // Remove from local state
      this.users = this.users.filter(u => u.id !== id);
    })
  );
}

// React
const deleteUser = async (userId) => {
  const confirmed = window.confirm('Are you sure you want to delete this user?');
  if (!confirmed) return;

  const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${userId}`, {
    method: 'DELETE',
    headers: { 'Authorization': 'Bearer token' }
  });

  if (response.status === 204) {
    console.log('User deleted successfully');
    return;
  }

  throw new Error('Failed to delete user');
};
```

