## Request & Response Structure

### Request Structure
```
GET /api/users/123?page=1 HTTP/1.1
Host: api.example.com
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer token123
Accept: application/json
X-Request-ID: req-456

{
  "filters": {
    "status": "active"
  }
}
```

**Components:**
- **Request Line**: Method, URI, HTTP version
- **Headers**: Metadata (Content-Type, Authorization, etc.)
- **Query Parameters**: URL parameters (?key=value)
- **Body**: Request payload (JSON, form data, etc.)

### Response Structure
```
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: 256
ETag: "abc123"
Cache-Control: max-age=3600
Date: Mon, 29 Dec 2024 10:00:00 GMT

{
  "id": 123,
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "createdAt": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z"
}
```

**Components:**
- **Status Line**: HTTP version, status code, reason phrase
- **Headers**: Metadata (Content-Type, ETag, Cache-Control, etc.)
- **Body**: Response payload

### Common Headers

**Request Headers:**
- `Content-Type`: Type of request body (application/json, multipart/form-data)
- `Accept`: Expected response format (application/json)
- `Authorization`: Authentication credentials (Bearer token)
- `X-Custom-Header`: Custom application headers
- `If-Match`: Conditional request (ETag matching)
- `If-Modified-Since`: Conditional request (timestamp)

**Response Headers:**
- `Content-Type`: Type of response body
- `Content-Length`: Size of response body
- `ETag`: Entity tag for caching
- `Cache-Control`: Caching directives (public, private, max-age)
- `Location`: URI of newly created resource (201 responses)
- `Set-Cookie`: Session/authentication cookies
- `X-RateLimit-Remaining`: Rate limit quota remaining

