## API Design Best Practices

### URI Design

**✓ Good Practices:**
```
GET /api/v1/users                          # Collection
GET /api/v1/users/123                      # Specific resource
GET /api/v1/users/123/orders               # Sub-resources
GET /api/v1/users?status=active&role=admin # Filtering
GET /api/v1/users?sort=name&page=2         # Sorting & pagination
```

**✗ Avoid:**
```
GET /api/getUsers                          # Don't use verb in URI
GET /api/user_list                         # Inconsistent naming
GET /api/users/123/getOrders               # Don't mix nouns and verbs
```

### Naming Conventions
```
/api/v1/users                    # Plural nouns
/api/v1/users/123/orders         # Lowercase, hyphens for compound words
/api/v1/user-preferences         # user-preferences not userPreferences
/api/v1/products?sort=price      # Query params for sorting/filtering
```

### Resource Organization
```
# User Management
GET    /api/v1/users              # List all users
POST   /api/v1/users              # Create new user
GET    /api/v1/users/123          # Get specific user
PUT    /api/v1/users/123          # Full update
PATCH  /api/v1/users/123          # Partial update
DELETE /api/v1/users/123          # Delete user

# User Orders (Sub-resource)
GET    /api/v1/users/123/orders   # Get user's orders
POST   /api/v1/users/123/orders   # Create order for user

# Search/Filtering (Alternative patterns)
GET    /api/v1/users/search?q=john
POST   /api/v1/users/search       # Complex filtering via POST
```

### Response Format Consistency
```javascript
// ✓ Consistent response structure
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "id": 123,
    "name": "John"
  },
  "meta": {
    "timestamp": "2024-12-29T10:00:00Z"
  }
}

// For lists
{
  "success": true,
  "data": [
    { "id": 1, "name": "John" },
    { "id": 2, "name": "Jane" }
  ],
  "pagination": {
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 10,
    "total": 100
  }
}

// For errors
{
  "success": false,
  "error": {
    "code": "INVALID_EMAIL",
    "message": "Email format is invalid",
    "details": {
      "field": "email",
      "value": "invalid"
    }
  }
}
```

### API Versioning Strategies
```
# Path versioning (Recommended)
GET /api/v1/users
GET /api/v2/users

# Header versioning
GET /api/users
Headers: API-Version: 1

# Query parameter versioning
GET /api/users?version=1

# Accept header
GET /api/users
Headers: Accept: application/vnd.company.v1+json
```

