## Authentication & Authorization

### Authentication (Who are you?)

#### 1. Basic Authentication
```
Authorization: Basic base64(username:password)
Authorization: Basic am9objphYmMxMjM=
```
**Pros**: Simple
**Cons**: Credentials in every request, no encryption (use HTTPS)

### 🔑 BASIC AUTH - KEY POINTS
```
✓ Simple to implement
✓ Works with all HTTP clients
✗ Credentials sent in every request
✗ No token expiration
✗ Requires HTTPS (always!)
⚠️ Never log or store plaintext passwords
```

### 💡 PRACTICAL EXAMPLES
```javascript
// Node.js - Basic Auth middleware
const basicAuth = (req, res, next) => {
  const auth = req.headers.authorization;
  
  if (!auth) {
    return res.status(401).json({
      error: { code: 'UNAUTHORIZED', message: 'No authorization header' }
    });
  }

  // Extract credentials
  const [scheme, credentials] = auth.split(' ');
  
  if (scheme !== 'Basic') {
    return res.status(400).json({
      error: { code: 'BAD_REQUEST', message: 'Invalid authorization scheme' }
    });
  }

  // Decode base64
  const decoded = Buffer.from(credentials, 'base64').toString();
  const [username, password] = decoded.split(':');

  // Validate credentials (in real app, check against DB)
  if (username !== 'admin' || password !== 'secret123') {
    return res.status(401).json({
      error: { code: 'INVALID_CREDENTIALS', message: 'Invalid username or password' }
    });
  }

  req.user = { username };
  next();
};

