## CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing)

### Same-Origin Policy
```
Same Origin:
- http://example.com/page1
- http://example.com/page2

Different Origin:
- http://example.com/
- http://subdomain.example.com/     (different subdomain)
- http://example.com:8080/          (different port)
- https://example.com/              (different protocol)

Browser blocks cross-origin requests by default
```

### CORS Headers

#### Simple Request (No Preflight)
```javascript
// Client request
GET http://example.com/api/data
Origin: http://localhost:3000

// Server response
Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://localhost:3000
Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true
```

#### Preflight Request (OPTIONS)
```javascript
// Browser sends OPTIONS first
OPTIONS /api/data
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Content-Type

// Server responds
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://localhost:3000
Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE
Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type, Authorization
Access-Control-Max-Age: 3600

// Then client sends actual request
POST /api/data
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: http://localhost:3000

{ "data": "..." }
```

### CORS Configuration Examples

**Express.js**
```javascript
const cors = require('cors');

// Allow all origins
app.use(cors());

// Allow specific origins
app.use(cors({
  origin: ['http://localhost:3000', 'http://example.com'],
  methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE'],
  credentials: true,
  maxAge: 3600
}));

// Custom logic
app.use(cors({
  origin: (origin, callback) => {
    const whitelist = ['http://localhost:3000', 'http://example.com'];
    if (whitelist.includes(origin) || !origin) {
      callback(null, true);
    } else {
      callback(new Error('Not allowed by CORS'));
    }
  }
}));
```

### CORS Request Types

**Simple Requests** (No preflight)
```
- Methods: GET, HEAD, POST
- Headers: Accept, Accept-Language, Content-Language
- Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded, multipart/form-data, text/plain
```

**Complex Requests** (Preflight required)
```
- Methods: PUT, DELETE, PATCH
- Custom headers
- Content-Type: application/json
- Authorization header
```

### CORS Issues & Solutions

**Issue: Request blocked**
```
Error: No 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header

Solution:
- Add CORS headers to server
- Add credentials: true if needed
- Whitelist origin on server
```

**Issue: Credentials not sent**
```
// Client
fetch(url, {
  credentials: 'include'  // Important!
})

// Server
Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true
```

