## 📚 QUICK REFERENCE CARDS

### HTTP Methods Decision Tree
```
Does it retrieve data?
  └─ YES → Use GET (safe, idempotent, cacheable)
  └─ NO → Create new resource?
           └─ YES → Use POST (returns 201 with Location)
           └─ NO → Update resource?
                    └─ Partial update? → Use PATCH
                    └─ Full replacement? → Use PUT
                    └─ Delete? → Use DELETE
```

### Status Code Selection Flow
```
Request successful?
├─ YES
│  ├─ Resource created (POST) → 201 Created
│  ├─ No content (DELETE) → 204 No Content
│  ├─ Conditional not met → 304 Not Modified
│  └─ Otherwise → 200 OK
└─ NO
   ├─ Client error?
   │  ├─ Malformed request → 400 Bad Request
   │  ├─ Auth required → 401 Unauthorized
   │  ├─ No permission → 403 Forbidden
   │  ├─ Not found → 404 Not Found
   │  ├─ Conflict/Duplicate → 409 Conflict
   │  └─ Rate limited → 429 Too Many Requests
   └─ Server error?
      ├─ Unexpected error → 500 Internal Server Error
      ├─ Not implemented → 501 Not Implemented
      ├─ Unavailable → 503 Service Unavailable
      └─ Timeout → 504 Gateway Timeout
```

### Authentication Comparison
| Method | Security | Complexity | Use Case |
|--------|----------|-----------|----------|
| Basic Auth | Low (use HTTPS) | Very Simple | Simple services, internal APIs |
| JWT | High | Medium | Stateless, microservices, SPAs |
| API Key | Medium | Simple | Server-to-server, backend services |
| OAuth 2.0 | High | Complex | Third-party integrations, user delegation |

### Caching Strategy Selection
```
Data changes frequently?
├─ YES
│  ├─ Critical consistency needed → Cache-Control: no-cache
│  └─ Some staleness ok → Cache-Control: max-age=60
└─ NO (static data)
   └─ Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
```

### Response Format Template
```javascript
// Success - Single resource
{
  "success": true,
  "data": { /* resource */ }
}

// Success - List
{
  "success": true,
  "data": [ /* resources */ ],
  "pagination": {
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 10,
    "total": 100,
    "pages": 10
  }
}

// Error
{
  "success": false,
  "error": {
    "code": "ERROR_CODE",
    "message": "Human-readable message",
    "details": { /* optional */ },
    "timestamp": "ISO-8601 timestamp",
    "requestId": "unique-id"
  }
}
```

