### 26. HATEOAS - THEORETICAL CONCEPT

**Definition**: Hypermedia As The Engine Of Application State.

**Concept**:
- Responses include links to related resources
- Client discovers state transitions through links
- No hardcoded URLs in clients
- Server controls possible actions

**HATEOAS Elements**:
- **Links**: References to related resources
- **Methods**: Available HTTP methods
- **Rel attribute**: Relationship type (self, next, previous, etc.)
- **Href**: Resource URI

**Example HATEOAS Response**:
```
{
  "id": 123,
  "name": "John",
  "links": [
    { "rel": "self", "href": "/api/users/123" },
    { "rel": "all-users", "href": "/api/users" },
    { "rel": "posts", "href": "/api/users/123/posts" }
  ]
}
```

**HATEOAS Benefits**:
- **Decoupling**: Clients don't need to know URI structure
- **Discoverability**: Clients find available actions
- **Evolution**: Server can change URIs without breaking clients
- **Flexibility**: Server can disable actions dynamically

**HATEOAS Challenges**:
- **Complexity**: More complex responses
- **Performance**: Extra data in responses
- **Adoption**: Most APIs don't implement it
- **Client complexity**: Requires more sophisticated clients

