#### Q5: What is idempotency?
**Answer:**
Idempotency means an operation produces the same result when called multiple times. Safe to retry without side effects.

**Idempotent methods:**
- GET: Always returns same result
- PUT: Replaces resource (multiple calls = same end state)
- DELETE: Removes resource (deleting again = same result)

**Non-idempotent:**
- POST: Creates new resource (multiple calls = multiple resources)
- PATCH: May not be idempotent

Example:
```javascript
// Idempotent - Safe to retry
PUT /api/users/123
{
  "name": "John",
  "email": "john@example.com"
}
// Called 3 times = same result (user updated once)

// Non-idempotent - NOT safe to retry
POST /api/users
{
  "name": "John",
  "email": "john@example.com"
}
// Called 3 times = 3 users created
```

