#### Q7: What is statelessness in REST?
**Answer:**
Statelessness means each request is independent and contains all information needed to process it. Server doesn't store client context between requests.

**Benefits:**
- Scalability: Any server can handle any request
- Reliability: Server crash doesn't affect client state
- Simplicity: No session management complexity

**Example:**

```javascript
// ✗ BAD - Stateful (NOT REST)
let currentUser;

app.post('/login', (req, res) => {
  currentUser = req.body.user; // Storing state!
  res.json({ success: true });
});

app.get('/data', (req, res) => {
  // Depends on previous request
  if (currentUser) {
    res.json(currentUser.data);
  }
});

// ✓ GOOD - Stateless (REST)
app.post('/login', (req, res) => {
  const token = jwt.sign(req.body.user, SECRET);
  res.json({ token }); // Return token
});

app.get('/data', (req, res) => {
  // Each request includes token
  const token = req.headers.authorization;
  const user = jwt.verify(token, SECRET);
  res.json(user.data);
});
```

